Z||000000||Huck||03-19-2001||12:32 AM||||Ok.  I'm confused.  Recently, my 87GT hasn't been running the smoothest.  It starts up and runs great when its cold, but as soon as it warms up it chuggs a lot under 2000rpm, and from a stop light its hard to get going unless you keep the rpm above 2000.  Also, when its warmed up, and you try to start it, it cranks over and over and doesnt fire.  Kinda like its flooded.  Brand new air filter in it, and the plugs are about 8,000km old.  <P>What gets me is how nice it still runs until it warms up.  Any suggestions folks?<P>Huck<BR>87GT T-top||||reg||5
Z||000001||862M4inCA||03-19-2001||02:59 AM||||hrm....I guess I'll start out with the obvious......Have you noticed the SES light come on? might even be a good idea to check for codes even if you haven't noticed. I'd also maybe be a little suspicious of the coolant and O2 sensors since those are "temp sensitive" and the ECM ignores them until they come up to temp.||||reg||1
